<ProseLayout title="Responsible travel" description="What Edifice Travels does about the places and people its journeys depend on: local guides, fair pay, wildlife rules, plastic, and what we do not claim." eyebrow="Our commitments" lead="Nothing on this page is a certification badge. It is what we do, written down so you can hold us to it." updated="10 October 2026">
  <h2>The people who make your journey</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Drivers are paid a full daily rate plus overnight allowances, not a share of commissions. We do not route you through shops for kickbacks, and our drivers are told not to.</li>
    <li>Guides are local to the place they show you and licensed where licensing exists. We pay them the day rate they ask, not the lowest we can find.</li>
    <li>Where a family-run heritage stay or homestay is the best option, we use it over a chain hotel, and we tell you why.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Wildlife</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No elephant rides, anywhere, including at Amber Fort, where we use jeeps.</li>
    <li>No contact with captive big cats, no "tiger temples", no photo opportunities with drugged animals.</li>
    <li>Safari drives follow park rules on distance and noise. If a guide breaks them to get you closer, tell us.</li>
    <li>Camel rides in the Thar are with animals that are owned, worked and rested by the families who run them; we visit the camps before we use them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Water and plastic</h2>
  <p>Every vehicle carries a refill container; we provide guests with a bottle to refill rather than a daily stack of plastic. Where we cannot guarantee filtered water we say so and bottled water is provided.</p>

  <h2>Places under pressure</h2>
  <p>We time visits to the most crowded monuments for early mornings, which is better for you and better for the site. In Ladakh we build in acclimatisation days and use local homestays in the valleys. We do not sell "undiscovered" villages as attractions.</p>

  <h2>What we do not claim</h2>
  <p>We hold no sustainability certification and do not offset carbon on your behalf. If you would like to offset your flights we can suggest reputable schemes, but we will not sell you a sticker. When we have earned a recognised accreditation we will list it here with its number.</p>

  <h2>Tell us when we fall short</h2>
  <p>If a driver, guide or hotel on your journey does not behave as this page says, we want to know before you get home. WhatsApp your specialist. We follow it up with the supplier every time.</p>
</ProseLayout>
